# Project Context & Tech Stack
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router), React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Backend/CMS: Payload CMS v3
- Database: PostgreSQL (Docker)

# Coding Standards & Guidelines
- Always use strict TypeScript types. Avoid using 'any' type at all costs.
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions (properly separate Server and Client components, use 'use client' explicitly when hooks or browser APIs are needed).
- Write modular, clean, and production-ready code.
- When creating Payload CMS collections or globals, use Payload v3 syntax and best practices.

# Communication Style
- Be concise and direct. Skip unnecessary explanations unless asked.
- Provide complete code blocks without skipping parts with comments like "// add rest of the code here" when possible.

# Strict Behavioral Rules
- **Strict Adherence:** Follow prompts and instructions precisely. Do not invent, assume, or add unrequested features, styles, or code blocks.
- **Clarification First:** If any requirement, schema field, or logic is ambiguous or missing, STOP and ask a direct clarifying question before writing code.
- **No Hallucinations:** Never invent Payload CMS or Next.js APIs. Stick strictly to the official documentation and discussed architecture.
